    "text": "hometownstations.com\nwebsite\nShelby County, Ohio\nMan rescued, hospitalized after Shelby County house fire\nBy Todd Cummins,\n8 hours agoSHELBY CO., OH (WLIO) – A Shelby County man was hospitalized for smoke inhalation after a house fire Wednesday afternoon. Around 12:30 p.m., Port Jefferson firefighters were called to 2990 Knoop Johnson Road in southeastern Shelby County. A male resident had to be rescued from the home and was taken to Wilson Health for treatment.\n1",
